	"identifying_description": "Ensemble: (a) short sleeved jacket of grey pinstripe wool embroidered with blue and pink floral designs and sequins; stand collar; trimmed with green fabric embellished with sequins; lined in silk (b) blouse of white cotton with masses of applied silver snaps as decoration; two pins attached to jacket of a snowflake and a bow.",
	"web_text": "“Dodie” Rosekrans was an early and enduring supporter of John Galliano’s work, financing collections as well as procuring some of his most iconic garments over more than fifteen years. The selection of whimsical designs seen here—which Galliano made under his eponymous label as well as while serving as creative director of the French couture house Christian Dior—were all worn by Rosekrans, who was recognized internationally for her eclectic style of dress.",
	"didactic_label": "“Dodie” Rosekrans was an early and enduring supporter of John Galliano’s work, financing collections as well as procuring some of his most iconic garments over more than fifteen years. The selection of whimsical designs seen here—which Galliano made under his eponymous label as well as while serving as creative director of the French couture house Christian Dior—were all worn by Rosekrans, who was recognized internationally for her eclectic style of dress.",
